{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>You guided with Your lovingkindness the people You redeemed; You led them with Your strength.</b> Rabbi Abraham ibn Ezra said that this is a past tense used in place of the future, for so it comes in the prophecies. In my opinion, the verse says: You stretched out Your right hand against the enemy, and the earth swallowed them — <b>and You guided with Your lovingkindness</b> by means of the pillar of cloud to lead them on the way — <b>the people You redeemed</b>, <b>and You led them</b> with the strength of Your hands <b>to Your holy habitation</b>, for toward it they journey. And similarly, 'and all the nations shall flow to it' (Isaiah 2:2). And 'Your holy habitation' is the Temple, as it says further on, 'The sanctuary, Adonai, which Your hands have established' (Exodus 15:17). And so they said in the Mekhilta (here): there is no 'habitation' (נוה) but the Temple, as it is stated, 'Behold Zion, the city of our appointed seasons; your eyes shall see Jerusalem, a quiet habitation' (Isaiah 33:20)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:08:31.095075271Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}